Here is an example of using a ViewBinding-generated layout file with AndroidViewBinding in AndroidView:

1. Create a layout file.

   ```xml
   <?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
   <androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout
       xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
       xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
       xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
       android:id="@+id/rootLayout"
       android:layout_width="match_parent"
       android:layout_height="match_parent">

       <!-- Add screen content here -->

   </androidx.constraintlayout.widget.ConstraintLayout>
   ```

2. Generate a ViewBinding class from the layout file by going to the menu bar and selecting `Tools` -> `Generate Layout File Bindings`.

3. Define the layout in the Compose file using the ViewBinding class.

   ```kotlin
   @Composable
   fun ExampleLayout() {
       val binding = ExampleBinding.inflate(LayoutInflateScope)</span>
       AndroidView(
           factory = { binding.root },
           modifier = Modifier,
           update = { state ->
               // Use the ViewBinding class to modify the view.
               binding.textView.text = state.text
               binding.button.setOnClickListener {
                   // Update the state of the Composable.
                   state.text = "Text updated!"
               }
           }
